<title>RUSSIA: Russia H1 privatisation revenue said 600 bln rbls.</title>
<headline>Russia H1 privatisation revenue said 600 bln rbls.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's revenue from privatisation in the first half of 1996 was some 600 billion roubles, Interfax news agency quoted a state property committee official as saying on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 1996 budget assumes revenue of 12 trillion roubles ($2.24 billion at current rates) for the full year.</p>
<p>First deputy chairman of the property committee Alfred Kokh said on Wednesday that sales of 25 percent of the Svyazinvest telecoms company and of shares in Unified Energy System could bring in up to $2.5 billion this year.</p>
<p>($=5363 roubles)</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
